<section id="research-software" data-index="Research software">
  <h2>Research software</h2>

  <div class="apps-grid">
    <div class="app-card">
      <h3>VSAX</h3>
      <p>A GPU-accelerated, JAX-native Python library for Vector Symbolic Architectures — composable, inspectable symbolic representations built from hypervectors. The legibility thread of my research, as code. <code>pip install vsax</code></p>
      <a href="https://vsarathy.com/vsax/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/vasanthsarathy/vsax" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="app-card">
      <h3>ArgLib</h3>
      <p>A Python library for warrant-gated argument graphs: typed claims, evidence, and credibility propagation. Contestable reasoning as a data structure — arguments you can audit, challenge, and defend.</p>
      <a href="https://vsarathy.com/arglib/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="app-card">
      <h3>delhi</h3>
      <p>An epistemic model checker in Rust: a language for describing what agents know and believe, how those attitudes shift as things happen, and how an agent ends up confidently wrong about what another agent believes. Reasoning about belief you can state as a formula and check, rather than take on faith. <code>cargo install delhi</code></p>
      <a href="https://vsarathy.com/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/vasanthsarathy/delhi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="app-card">
      <h3>Crucible</h3>
      <p>A Claude Code plugin for review-driven AI/ML research: your work passes staged gates before a panel of nine adversarial reviewer personas. Treat reviewers like tests — the adversarial-evaluation stance, turned on my own research process.</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/vasanthsarathy/crucible" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

